33:<h3>Separate detector exposures and continuous pointing</h3><p>Each detector row averages the selected model over that detector’s actual accepted GTIs on the selected comparison clock. The continuous row averages the whole published pointing, including gaps rejected by individual detectors. Simultaneous MOS1/MOS2/PN exposure seconds are not elapsed observing time and cannot be combined into an EPIC mean without detector-response weighting. The PN lead curve, manuscript comparison and registered convergence measures remain PN-GTI based.</p>
